# Everything listed here is excluded from the build context, so it never
# reaches the Docker daemon and can never end up in an image layer.

# Version control metadata. Keeping .git out also means `go build` has no VCS to
# stamp, which is why the builder stage passes -buildvcs=false.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode

# Local build output and test artifacts
engine
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
*.log

# Runtime data. The runtime stage creates its own empty /app/storage.
storage

# Container and project docs
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
compose*.yml
README.md
LICENSE

# Tests are not needed to compile the binary
**/*_test.go

# NOTE: .env and .env.test are deliberately NOT ignored. They stay available so
# `--build-arg ENV_FILE=.env` works. The builder stage copies only cmd/ and
# internal/, so env files are read solely by the runtime stage.
